Yes. The current official Responses API schema supports outbound network access for an automatically created Code Interpreter container via an allowlist.

**Exact schema declaration:**

> `network_policy: optional ContainerNetworkPolicyDisabled { type } or ContainerNetworkPolicyAllowlist { allowed_domains, type, domain_secrets }`

The allowlist variant has `type: "allowlist"`, required `allowed_domains`, and optional `domain_secrets`. ([developers.openai.com](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/__sdk_schema?declaration=%28resource%29+responses+%3E+%28model%29+container_auto+%3E+%28schema%29&selected=%28resource%29+responses))

Usable Responses API tool shape:

```json
{
  "type": "code_interpreter",
  "container": {
    "type": "container_auto",
    "network_policy": {
      "type": "allowlist",
      "allowed_domains": [
        "api.example.com"
      ],
      "domain_secrets": [
        {
          "domain": "api.example.com",
          "name": "API_KEY",
          "value": "secret-value"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

`domain_secrets` is optional; omit it when authentication injection is unnecessary. Only domains listed in `allowed_domains` receive outbound access. The separate Containers API documents the same `allowlist` policy and provides an official example using `api.buildkite.com`. ([developers.openai.com](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/containers/methods/create))
